<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diomedes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diomedes was a Greek hero of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trojan-war">Trojan War</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> and one of the bravest fighters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iliad">Iliad</a>. Later legend told that on his return from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a> he sailed to southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and founded Arpi and other towns in Daunia, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>. The Daunians and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> accepted the story, and he was worshipped as a hero in several places around the Adriatic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diomedes.jpg" alt="Diomedes" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Copy of Nausykles or Kresilas (?) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diomedes_Louvre_Ma890_n3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
